  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU-UN Support to the States in Central Asia for their Citizens Returned from Conflict Zones - Component I - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;ordered&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; background-color: white;&quot;&gt;Children and their mothers/caregivers repatriated from conflict zones benefit from child and human rights-based, age and gender-sensitive &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;support for recovery and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; background-color: white;&quot;&gt;reintegration into society. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;ordered&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black; background-color: white;&quot;&gt;National and local capacities are strengthened to meet the needs of returned children and their families throughout the reintegration and recovery process &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-list=&quot;ordered&quot; class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ql-ui&quot; contenteditable=&quot;false&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Practices, lessons and approaches are shared across the region and coordinated amongst UN agencies, EU institutions and practitioners supporting reintegration and recovery, and opportunities for sub-regional learning and cooperation exist. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
